---
description: Do not widen cardFactory/segFactory returns to ICard/ISeg
alwaysApply: true
---

# Infer Factory Return Types

Do **not** annotate functions that return `cardFactory` / `segFactory` results as `ICard` or `ISeg`. That widens the return to the base interface and drops preprocessor-generated `GenCards` / `GenSegments` inference (attrs, nested, typed `selfPos`).

Prefer an inferred return. When a named type is required, use generated `GenCardTypes.<TypeName>` / `GenSegTypes.<TypeName>` — not the widened base interface.

Composite layout/model objects (cards + segments + controllers) use an explicit interface, not `ReturnType<typeof createLayout>`. See [No ReturnType Aliases](no-returntype.mdc).

Incorrect:

```typescript
export function createRequestedMatrixCard(entries: RequestedEntry[]): ICard {
  return cardFactory({
    typeName: "RequestedListCard",
    nested: eMappedFactory(collection, (entry) =>
      cardFactory({ typeName: "RequestedCellCard", attrs, selfPos: { /* ... */ } }),
    ),
  });
}
```

Correct:

```typescript
export function createRequestedMatrixCard(entries: RequestedEntry[]) {
  return cardFactory({
    typeName: "RequestedListCard",
    nested: eMappedFactory(collection, (entry) =>
      cardFactory({ typeName: "RequestedCellCard", attrs, selfPos: { /* ... */ } }),
    ),
  });
}
```

See [README Infer factory returns](../../README.md#infer-factory-returns).
